@KafkaConsumerMicroService_HostAddress = http://localhost:5251

### Sample CSV file (create sample.csv in the same folder for testing)
###
### SourceSystem,AccountNumber,PnLAmount
### XFeed,1234,100.5
### RealtimeBus,2345,0.0
### ExtSystem,3456,-50.25
###

GET {{KafkaConsumerMicroService_HostAddress}}/weatherforecast/
Accept: application/json

###
### Get OpenAPI JSON (HTTP)
GET {{KafkaConsumerMicroService_HostAddress}}/openapi
Accept: application/json

###

### Open API UI (browser)
GET {{KafkaConsumerMicroService_HostAddress}}/openapi/ui
Accept: text/html

###

### Health ping
GET {{KafkaConsumerMicroService_HostAddress}}/api/health/ping
Accept: application/json

###

### Recent valid records
GET {{KafkaConsumerMicroService_HostAddress}}/api/health/valid-records
Accept: application/json

###

### Recent invalid records
GET {{KafkaConsumerMicroService_HostAddress}}/api/health/invalid-records
Accept: application/json

###

### Demo UI (SignalR client)
GET {{KafkaConsumerMicroService_HostAddress}}/demo.html
Accept: text/html


### Upload CSV using curl (use -k for dev self-signed certs)
# curl -k -X POST "https://localhost:7023/api/ingest/csv" -F "file=@./sample.csv"

### Upload CSV using REST Client (multipart). Save sample.csv next to this file and run.
POST {{KafkaConsumerMicroService_HostAddress}}/api/ingest/csv
Content-Type: multipart/form-data

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

SourceSystem,AccountNumber,PnLAmount
XFeed,1234,100.5
RealtimeBus,2345,0.0
ExtSystem,3456,-50.25

--boundary--

